the holy roman empire was a staple of  european politics throughout the  entirety of the middle ages  its emperors held positions of immense  influence which they maintained until  1806 when napoleon happened  yet given the importance of the holy  roman empire historically why was it  dissolved why did the holy roman empire  come to an end and why did nobody do  anything about it  so by 1806 europe had been plagued by  near constant war with france for over a  decade and napoleon now the emperor of  france had plans to reforge europe in  france's image and interests  strangely enough many of europe's rulers  opposed this and so were currently  fighting a war against france as a  coalition to crush napoleon once and for  all but fun fact  no napoleon and his generals had  routinely defeated the coalition allies  and in 1805 they thoroughly crushed the  austrians at the battle of austerlitz  soon after this austria made peace with  france and napoleon was essentially  given free reign to rearrange central  europe how he pleased  this led him creating the confederation  of the rhine the next year which was a  collective of german states who in  return for some territorial  consolidation were to be french puppets  and fight when napoleon asked  furthermore napoleon granted himself the  title of protector of the confederation  of the rhine  and to many this second power structure  within the holy roman empire was  essentially its practical end since  their allegiance was now to paris and  not vienna  the current holy roman emperor francis  ii believed that napoleon was coming for  his title  as such francis did the only thing that  he could he announced his abdication and  as his last act he dissolved the holy  roman empire  whilst he absolutely had the right to do  the abdicating bit it was less clear  whether or not he had the authority to  abolish the empire as a whole  despite the fact it was a gray area and  the empire did  so why did everyone just go along with  it the reason why other german states  and rulers were fine with it was that  the title of holy roman emperor was by  this point ceremonial  the holy roman emperor couldn't levy  armies prevent his subjects from making  foreign alliances or even stop a certain  naughtier subject from warring against  the emperor himself if they wanted to  the fact was that the existence of the  holy roman empire was by and large  irrelevant to the everyday running of  its constituent states  and for the remaining german rulers in  the confederation of the rind the new  system had just allowed them to swallow  up some of their smaller neighbors with  no problems  so for them it was definitely a win even  if napoleon had more oversight than the  emperor did so what about napoleon the  only man who could have if he wished  simply declared the empire to still  exist  well whilst he could have taken the  title for himself he had no reason to  the confederation of the rhyme was  largely a buffer state against  austria prussia and russia whereas  maintaining the holy roman empire  wouldn't have provided the same security  because prussia in austria could  potentially tip the internal balance of  power  he also had no reason to oppose its  abolition in the end of the empire his  new europe didn't need what many  saw as a bloated inefficient relic of  the medieval era and  importantly without a holy roman emperor  who also helped the title of king in  germany there was no central figure that  the german states could rally around and  oppose him  now they had to side with either himself  the king of prussia or the emperor of  austria  and of those last two those in the  confederation of the rhine had no reason  to side with austria whereas many of  them had much to fear from prussia  and so the holy roman empire died not  with any fanfare or conflict but simply  because nobody cared enough to save it  the last emperor declared his title  abolished and ultimately nobody else  wanted it  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons  james bissonette kelly moneymaker marvin  castle mo aaron the white  james castaneda marcus arsenal jordan  longley gustav swann rasheed ali  jerry lambda maggie patzkowski  coppertone winston cayward spencer  lightfoot robert wetzel spinning three  plates corso wolff matthew shipley  anthony beckett and charles the first  you
 

